   "tutor": "Here's the rule: after he, she or it, the verb takes -s, -es (watches) or -ies (cries).\nRight: \"The robot washes the floor.\" Wrong: \"The robot wash the floor.\" The robot is it, so the verb needs an ending.\nLet me think aloud: \"The robot fixes cars.\" The robot is it. Fix ends in x, so I add -es.\nYour turn. Is the person he, she or it? Then write the verb:\nWrite the correct form: My sister ___ (play) tennis on Sundays. (answer with only the verb)",
